---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import MicrosoftFormEmbed from '../../components/MicrosoftFormEmbed.astro';
import { INITIAL_SUBMISSION_FORM_URL } from '../../config/forms.ts';
---

<BaseLayout title="Enter">
  <h1>Enter — Initial Submission</h1>

  <p class="lede">
    The initial submission is a <strong>prototype / proof of concept</strong>,
    not a finished app — we're evaluating your idea and your approach, so
    don't let polish get in the way of a strong concept. Submissions open
    <strong>Friday 11 September 2026</strong> and close at the prototype
    deadline, <strong>Friday 4 December 2026</strong> (23:59 UTC&minus;12, so
    the deadline has passed everywhere in the world).
  </p>

  <p>
    Before you start, it's worth reading the <a href="/judging/">judging
    criteria</a> and the <a href="/programme-data/">Programme Data</a> page.
    You can't save and return to the form partway through, so prepare your
    answers first using the question list below. You'll need a working demo
    link, a walkthrough video link, and a public code repository URL.
  </p>

  <section>
    <h2>What you'll be asked</h2>
    <p>The form has five sections:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Your team</strong> — team name, lead contact name and
        email, a list of all team members with affiliation (one per line,
        in the format <em>Name — Affiliation</em>), country or region, and
        a conflict-of-interest declaration if anyone on the team is a
        CHI&nbsp;2027 author, committee member, or organiser.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your app</strong> — app name, a link to a square app icon
        (min. 512×512px, committed to your repository), a tagline (max 80
        characters), a one-line description (max 150 characters), a full
        description (max 500 words), and which attendees the app is for.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Your app and your code</strong> — a live public URL for
        your working app (no login or invitation required), the URL of
        your public git repository, your open source licence, and a
        walkthrough video link (max 5 minutes). Both the app and the
        repository must stay accessible until at least the end of
        January&nbsp;2027.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Technical and legal</strong> — third-party libraries, APIs,
        models, and AI tools used; what personal data (if any) your app
        collects or processes; an intellectual property confirmation; and
        a commitment to comply with CHI's data protection requirements
        once shared with you.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Optional extras</strong> — accessibility features
        (implemented and planned), details of any LLM or AI components,
        and anything else the judges should know, such as which parts of
        your demo are functional versus mocked up.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Note: file uploads aren't collected via the form — since every
      submission is open source, the icon and any other assets should live
      in your repository and be linked from there.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Submit</h2>
    <MicrosoftFormEmbed
      formUrl={INITIAL_SUBMISSION_FORM_URL}
      title="CHI 2027 Digital Experience Competition — Initial Submission"
    />
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .lede {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
  }

  section {
    margin: 2.25rem 0;
  }

  section h2 {
    color: var(--color-navy);
  }
</style>
